From 3ac83b2847f151af6deb366560a01c114b080f92 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: HampterDev <131729366+HampterDev@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 23:21:38 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Forget the private-airplane window when it is destroyed

open_airship (navigation_cmd.c) keeps the private-airplane window in
g_windowMgr.private_airplane_wnd for its modal loop, outside the window
lists, and clears the slot only when the loop ends with
AIRPLANE_RESULT_CLOSED (0xb4: the close button, Escape, a teardown or
the server's accept). A flight ends it otherwise: the airplane map move
goes through game_mode_zc_npcack_mapmove, which sets modal_result to
0xb1. The loop then posts the window to the quit list, the window is
destroyed at the end of the frame, and the slot kept pointing at it
until the next map's mode init cleared all slots. In that time nothing
dereferences it: key_down only tests it, and
game_mode_on_ack_private_airplane_call, which sends it a message, runs
from the network poll at the start of a frame, while the window is
destroyed in the input step of the same frame and the next frame
belongs to the new map's mode. ui_window_destruct calls ui_window_mgr_forget_window for every
window; the slot is now in its list, so it is cleared with the window.

The other three slots named with it have no such path:
- hot_key_wnd is closed through post_quit1(0x9c), which clears it, also
  for its own OK and close buttons (ui_close_window(WND_HOTKEY)).
- quest_display_wnd is closed through close_slot (0xcc).
- drag_plate is closed through ui_window_mgr_close_drag_plate,
  ui_window_mgr_set_drag_plate (which replaces it) and the close of
  windows 0x22 and 0x45 in window_slots.c, which all clear or replace
  it; it is in the window list but not in the plate list, so the plate
  paths do not destroy it.
None of them closes itself or is a child of another window, and both
close-all paths clear all four through clear_slots. They are left out.

The new test_airplane_window_slot runs the slot statements extracted
from open_airship around the extracted modal loop (ui_window_mgr_do_modal,
run_modal, ui_window_mgr_modal_loop) with one frame that ends the loop,
then destroys the posted window through the extracted ui_window_destruct
and the real forget_window.c. Ended by closing (0xb4) the slot is cleared
either way; ended by the flight's map move (0xb1) it fails on the
previous list ("private_airplane_wnd still points at the destroyed
window").

